# Project Scope Statement

## Project Title

Personal Portfolio Website

## Project Purpose

The purpose of this project is to create a simple personal portfolio website that introduces who I am, my education, skills, professional interests, and future career goals. This project will also allow me to practice the skills I have learned throughout CMPA 3301, including HTML, CSS, GitHub, project planning, documentation, and managing changes during a project.

Another purpose of the website is to create something that can continue to be useful after this course. I want to have a basic portfolio that I can improve as I complete more projects and gain more experience. In the future, I could potentially share the website when applying for internships or jobs in a STEM-related field.

## Description

The final product will be a two-page personal portfolio website hosted through GitHub Pages. The homepage will introduce me and explain the purpose of the portfolio. It will also provide a quick overview of my professional interests and goals.

The second page will provide more information about my education, skills, experience, and career goals. Both pages will use the same external CSS stylesheet so the website has a consistent appearance and design.

The GitHub repository will also include project documentation. This documentation will explain the scope of the project, project plan, risks, task schedule, and a retrospective about the overall project process.

## Desired Results

The desired result is a working and organized website that is easy to navigate and represents me professionally. The website should demonstrate that I understand the basic concepts of HTML and CSS and can organize a small digital project using GitHub.

By the end of the project, I want to have:

- A working two-page website.
- Consistent styling across both pages.
- Navigation between the homepage and About page.
- A public GitHub repository that is organized clearly.
- A live website published with GitHub Pages.
- Complete project management documentation.
- A project that can be expanded later as I gain more skills and experience.

## Exclusions

This project will remain simple because the main goal is to demonstrate the skills learned during the course. The project will not include advanced JavaScript, databases, user accounts, login systems, online payments, or other advanced web development features.

The website will also not include every project or job experience I have ever completed. Instead, it will focus on a basic introduction and information that is relevant to my education and professional goals. Additional projects and features can be added in the future, but they are outside the scope of this version.

## Project Constraints

One of the biggest constraints is time because I am completing the project while balancing other school assignments and work responsibilities. Another constraint is my current experience with GitHub and web development. I have improved throughout the course, but I am still learning how GitHub, GitHub Pages, HTML, and CSS work together.

Because of these constraints, keeping the project simple and organized is important. The main priority is completing all required parts and making sure the website works correctly.
